WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.474 --> 00:00:08.140
&gt;&gt; Greg: TODAY IS TAKE YOUR

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:10.242
CHILD TO WORK DAY, EMPHASIS ON

00:00:10.243 --> 00:00:10.542
YOUR.

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:12.411
GET THAT WRONG AND IT COULD BE

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:13.345
TAKE YOURSELF TO JAIL DAY.

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:15.280
A HALF OF ME HATES THIS DAY.

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:16.915
I DON'T LIKE SHARING THE

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:17.983
ELEVATOR WITH PEOPLE WERE

00:00:17.984 --> 00:00:20.552
ONE-TENTH MY AGE AND 100% MY

00:00:20.553 --> 00:00:21.620
HEIGHT.

00:00:21.621 --> 00:00:22.354
PLUS IT MEANS DANA HAS TO WATCH

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:24.156
HER LANGUAGE IN THE HALLS AND WE

00:00:24.157 --> 00:00:26.325
ALL KNOW HOW FILTHY SHE IS.

00:00:26.326 --> 00:00:27.526
IT'S HARD TO FIRE SOMEONE WHO IS

00:00:27.527 --> 00:00:28.527
THEIR KID WITH THEM.

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:30.229
HOW DO YOU DO THAT?

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:32.331
TELL THE PARENT TO WAIT OUTSIDE

00:00:32.332 --> 00:00:33.766
AND TELL YOUR KID -- THE KID

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:35.934
YOUR DAD IS FIRED.

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:37.669
TAKE YOUR CHILD TO WORK DAY HAS

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:39.905
BECOME THE DAY YOU CAN'T SWEAR

00:00:39.906 --> 00:00:41.707
OR FIRE ANYONE.

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:43.008
PEOPLE LIKE DANA WHO ENJOYS

00:00:43.009 --> 00:00:44.877
SWEARING AND MAKING PEOPLE CRY.

00:00:44.878 --> 00:00:46.712
I DON'T HAVE KIDS SO TODAY IS NO

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:48.247
DIFFERENT THAN YESTERDAY EXCEPT

00:00:48.248 --> 00:00:49.214
WITH MORE SCREAMING WHICH SCARES

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:51.116
THE KIDS WHEN I DO IT.

00:00:51.117 --> 00:00:52.417
THE OTHER HALF OF ME EMBRACES

00:00:52.418 --> 00:00:53.252
THIS DAY.

00:00:53.253 --> 00:00:55.020
IT'S GOOD THAT YOUR KIDS SEE

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:57.122
WHAT PEOPLE DO FOR A LIVING.

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:59.525
THEY NEED TO LEARN THAT MONEY

00:00:59.526 --> 00:01:00.259
ISN'T SOMETHING THAT

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:01.493
MYSTERIOUSLY REGENERATES IN THE

00:01:01.494 --> 00:01:01.827
WALLET.

00:01:01.828 --> 00:01:03.462
MOM AND DAD HAVE TO WORK TO PAY

00:01:03.463 --> 00:01:06.732
FOR YOUR CLOTHES, YOUR TOYS,

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:07.432
YOUR WORTHLESS POLITICALLY

00:01:07.433 --> 00:01:09.334
CORRECT OVERPRICED EDUCATION.

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:11.303
WORK IS OFTEN THE THING YOU KNOW

00:01:11.304 --> 00:01:12.738
LEAST ABOUT YOUR PARENTS.

00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:14.473
I REMEMBER MY DAD TAKING ME TO

00:01:14.474 --> 00:01:16.208
WORK, AND IT WAS THRILLING.

00:01:16.209 --> 00:01:17.943
I DROVE THE GETAWAY CAR.

00:01:17.944 --> 00:01:19.511
THAT'S WHERE I LEARNED ABOUT THE

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:21.146
MAGICAL MONEY IN THE WALLET.

00:01:21.147 --> 00:01:23.282
IT'S GREAT TO SEE ANOTHER PLACE

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:23.982
WHERE YOUR PARENTS OR SOMEBODY

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:24.817
ELSE OR NOT IN A BATHROOM.

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:28.687
THEY HAD A ROLE OUTSIDE YOUR

00:01:28.688 --> 00:01:30.088
WORLD.

00:01:30.089 --> 00:01:31.623
YOUR PARENTS AREN'T JUST PARENTS

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:33.091
BUT HUMAN BEINGS HATED BY OTHER

00:01:33.092 --> 00:01:33.525
HUMAN BEINGS.

00:01:33.526 --> 00:01:37.729
ENJOY THE DAY BUT IF YOUR CAN

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:38.430
TOUCH AS ANYTHING ON DESK,

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:41.967
YOU'RE DEAD.

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:45.470
THEY MADE EARTH DAY EARTH WEEK.

00:01:45.471 --> 00:01:46.238
TODAY IS TAKE YOUR CHILD TO WORK

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:48.440
SO HAVE COMBINED IT.

00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:50.876
I TAKE MY PLANT TO WORK.

00:01:50.877 --> 00:01:53.679
&gt;&gt; Dana: DID YOU CARRY IT ALL

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:54.847
DAY?

00:01:54.848 --> 00:01:55.447
&gt;&gt; Greg: THAT'S TYLER.

00:01:55.448 --> 00:02:04.723
IT  &gt;&gt; Jesse: LOOKS DRY, LET ME

00:02:04.724 --> 00:02:05.490
WATER IT.

00:02:05.491 --> 00:02:06.992
&gt;&gt; Dana: MILES, THE

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:08.894
4-MONTH-OLD SON OF ONE OF OUR

00:02:08.895 --> 00:02:09.261
PRODUCERS.

00:02:09.262 --> 00:02:14.199
I SAW A COUPLE OF OTHER KIDS.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.501
&gt;&gt; Greg: A 4-MONTH-OLD?

00:02:16.502 --> 00:02:17.936
&gt;&gt; Dana: HE'S NEVER COME TO

00:02:17.937 --> 00:02:19.438
VISIT US.

00:02:19.439 --> 00:02:20.505
&gt;&gt; Greg: THE BABY IS NOT GOING

00:02:20.506 --> 00:02:21.006
TO LEARN ANYTHING.

00:02:21.007 --> 00:02:24.776
&gt;&gt; Dana: THEY ARE STARTING

00:02:24.777 --> 00:02:28.380
EARLY.

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:32.217
&gt;&gt; Jesse: THE BABY ON YOUR

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:32.517
DESK.

00:02:32.518 --> 00:02:33.285
&gt;&gt; Dana: BRINGING KIDS TO WORK

00:02:33.286 --> 00:02:36.255
ONE DAY A YEAR IS A GOOD THING.

00:02:36.256 --> 00:02:37.823
&gt;&gt; Greg: I DISAGREE.

00:02:37.824 --> 00:02:39.324
I THINK, JUAN, AND SHOULD NOT BE

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:40.525
AN ORCHESTRATED THING.

00:02:40.526 --> 00:02:42.027
BUT YOUR KID WHENEVER YOU WANT.

00:02:42.028 --> 00:02:44.162
IT'S MORE EXCITING.

00:02:44.163 --> 00:02:45.330
&gt;&gt; Dana: YOU THINK THAT WOULD

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:48.600
BE BETTER THAN ONE DAY?

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:50.035
&gt;&gt; Greg: I WAS A CHILD BEFORE

00:02:50.036 --> 00:02:51.236
THIS FAKE HOLIDAY.

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:52.271
MY DAD WAS AN ACCOUNTANT.

00:02:52.272 --> 00:02:56.775
IT WAS THRILLING TO ME.

00:02:56.776 --> 00:02:59.411
CALCULATOR.

00:02:59.412 --> 00:02:59.878
1970.

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:01.179
&gt;&gt; Juan: THAT THING I REMEMBER

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:03.916
ABOUT THIS, I TOOK MY DAUGHTER.

00:03:03.917 --> 00:03:05.751
SHE WAS AT MY DESK AT

00:03:05.752 --> 00:03:06.852
"THE WASHINGTON POST."

00:03:06.853 --> 00:03:08.253
SHE KEPT THAT PICTURE FOREVER.

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:09.454
WOW.

00:03:09.455 --> 00:03:10.889
IT WAS A BIG DEAL TO HER.

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:11.657
SEE WHERE YOUR DAD WORKS.

00:03:11.658 --> 00:03:13.592
&gt;&gt; Dana: YOU ARE GONE ALL THE

00:03:13.593 --> 00:03:14.059
TIME.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:14.860
WHERE IS HE?

00:03:14.861 --> 00:03:16.428
&gt;&gt; Greg: THIS IS WHERE DAD

00:03:16.429 --> 00:03:17.930
GOES TO PAY FOR THAT FOOD.

00:03:17.931 --> 00:03:20.599
&gt;&gt; Juan: I WISH THEY MADE THAT

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:21.033
CONNECTION.

00:03:21.034 --> 00:03:21.466
I'M NOT SURE.

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:23.001
&gt;&gt; Jesse: I SAW MY DAUGHTER

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:24.636
TODAY AND SHE ASKED ME IF I HAD

00:03:24.637 --> 00:03:27.005
MORE THAN $1,000 IN MY BANK

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:27.673
ACCOUNT.

00:03:27.674 --> 00:03:28.040
[LAUGHTER]

00:03:28.041 --> 00:03:28.907
SHE THINKS IT'S A LOT OF MONEY.

00:03:28.908 --> 00:03:30.442
I SAID YES, I DO.

00:03:30.443 --> 00:03:31.510
SHE WAS REALLY IMPRESSED.

00:03:31.511 --> 00:03:34.346
IT MADE ME FEEL GREAT.

00:03:34.347 --> 00:03:37.082
&gt;&gt; Dana: WHAT DID SHE WANT TO

00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:37.916
BUY?

00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:39.818
&gt;&gt; Jesse: WILL FIND OUT LATER.

00:03:39.819 --> 00:03:41.253
I DIDN'T SEE ANY KIDS AT WORK

00:03:41.254 --> 00:03:44.356
TODAY BECAUSE I GOT HERE AT 4:3

00:03:44.357 --> 00:03:44.656
4:30.

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:46.458
&gt;&gt; Dana: SO YOU DIDN'T REALLY

00:03:46.459 --> 00:03:46.858
WORK TODAY?

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:49.294
&gt;&gt; Jesse: I WAS WITH THE KIDS

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:50.429
ALL DAY!

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:53.031
&gt;&gt; Dana: CAN I GET THAT DEAL?

00:03:53.032 --> 00:03:53.699
&gt;&gt; Greg: THEY ARE GOING TO

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:55.434
PLAY THIS BACK.

00:03:55.435 --> 00:03:58.804
COMES IN AT 4:30.

00:03:58.805 --> 00:04:01.206
&gt;&gt; Jesse: I LISTENED TO RUSH

00:04:01.207 --> 00:04:01.573
LIMBAUGH.

00:04:01.574 --> 00:04:02.307
&gt;&gt; Greg: EMILY, WHAT ARE YOUR

00:04:02.308 --> 00:04:03.208
THOUGHTS?

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:04.376
YOU ARE YOUNG ENOUGH THAT YOU

00:04:04.377 --> 00:04:05.143
PROBABLY WANT TO TAKE YOUR CHILD

00:04:05.144 --> 00:04:07.079
TO WORK DAY.

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:09.081
&gt;&gt; Jesse: DID SOMEONE TAKE YOU

00:04:09.082 --> 00:04:09.514
TO WORK TODAY?

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:11.383
&gt;&gt; Emily: I AM OLDER THAN YOU

00:04:11.384 --> 00:04:11.683
ARE.

00:04:11.684 --> 00:04:20.225
MY MOM WAS A LIBRARIAN.

00:04:20.226 --> 00:04:21.860
&gt;&gt; Greg: IT'S LIKE QUINCY

00:04:21.861 --> 00:04:22.427
MEETS --

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:23.528
&gt;&gt; Emily: MY LUNCH BAG WAS A

00:04:23.529 --> 00:04:27.232
SPECIMEN BAG.

00:04:27.233 --> 00:04:28.900
LATER I REALIZE HOW ODD IT WAS.

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:32.037
FOR ORGANS AND STUFF.

00:04:32.038 --> 00:04:33.238
IT KEPT MY FOOD COLD.

00:04:33.239 --> 00:04:34.639
MY POINT IS WE SHOULD HAVE A

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:36.575
BRING YOUR DOG TO WORK DAY.

00:04:36.576 --> 00:04:37.275
&gt;&gt; Dana: THEY DO HAVE ABOUT

00:04:37.276 --> 00:04:39.711
SOME WORKPLACES.

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:42.280
&gt;&gt; Jesse: I FORGET IS THIS

00:04:42.281 --> 00:04:42.848
FRIDAY.

00:04:42.849 --> 00:04:43.782
&gt;&gt; Emily: AT FOX?

00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:45.017
&gt;&gt; Jesse: BRING YOUR DOG TO

00:04:45.018 --> 00:04:45.751
WORK DAY.

00:04:45.752 --> 00:04:46.184
ONE IS THAT?

00:04:46.185 --> 00:04:53.925
SOMEONE JUST TOLD ME.

00:04:53.926 --> 00:04:55.460
&gt;&gt; Dana: BEING RAISED AS A

00:04:55.461 --> 00:04:56.261
SERVICE DOG.

00:04:56.262 --> 00:04:58.430
IT'S NOT LIKE BRINGING JASPER TO

00:04:58.431 --> 00:04:59.865
WORK.

00:04:59.866 --> 00:05:01.099
&gt;&gt; Emily: IF WE ALL DID IT AT

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:04.069
ONCE IT WOULD BE GREAT.

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:05.537
&gt;&gt; Greg: WHAT HAPPENS TO THE

00:05:05.538 --> 00:05:06.438
ROBOTS?

00:05:06.439 --> 00:05:08.373
WHAT WILL THEY BRING TO WORK?

00:05:08.374 --> 00:05:08.740
A TOASTER?

00:05:08.741 --> 00:05:11.109
LITTLE ROBOTS.

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:11.977
A TINY CIRCUIT.

00:05:11.978 --> 00:05:15.180
&gt;&gt; Juan: THE BAG, I HOPE YOU

00:05:15.181 --> 00:05:20.952
DIDN'T GET A LIVER SANDWICH.

00:05:20.953 --> 00:05:21.586
&gt;&gt; Greg: YOU HAVE TO ASK

00:05:21.587 --> 00:05:22.320
YOURSELF IF YOUR KID CAN'T COME

00:05:22.321 --> 00:05:24.656
TO YOUR PLACE OF WORK.

00:05:24.657 --> 00:05:26.592
&gt;&gt; Jesse: CERTAIN PLACES CAN'T

